-- The tree says each thing once. A node names its role (term), its word's iʿrāb link its case and sign; a note is for
-- what neither says. Cleaned here, the rows themselves:
-- 1. qr_114's head nodes carried a note that only repeated their chip (مضاف): gone.
-- 2. A phrase whose head is its own مضاف node no longer stands for the head's word — the head does (the word's
--    case is shown once, on it).
-- 3. 154 notes opened by restating the node's role and case («مضاف إليه مجرور؛ الإضافة محضة فتفيد التعريف»): each
--    keeps only what it adds («الإضافة محضة فتفيد التعريف»), and 148 that said nothing else are cleared. Each update
--    is guarded on the note as it stood, so an edited note is left; swap the two texts to restore any.
UPDATE qr_ss_tree_node SET label_ar = NULL WHERE id LIKE '%.mudaf' AND label_ar = 'مضاف';
UPDATE qr_ss_tree_node AS p SET word_occurrence_id = NULL
 WHERE p.word_occurrence_id IS NOT NULL
   AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM qr_ss_tree_node c
                WHERE c.parent_node_id = p.id AND c.word_occurrence_id = p.word_occurrence_id
                  AND COALESCE(c.gram_term_ref, c.term_key) IN ('GT:irab_role:mudaf', 'mudaf'));
